      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n, s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\n\t// Flatten matrix into a contiguous 1D array for better spatial locality\n\tconst int np1 = n + 1; // size of prefix sum dimension (extra row/col of zeros)\n\tstd::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Integral image (summed-area table) using long long to avoid overflow\n\tstd::vector<long long> pref(np1 * np1, 0LL);\n\n\t// First pass: horizontal cumulative sums per row\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\t\tlong long row_sum = 0;\n\t\tconst int base_i = (i + 1) * np1;\n\t\tconst int mat_base = i * n;\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\trow_sum += mat[mat_base + j];\n\t\t\tpref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Second pass: vertical accumulation to complete the integral image\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\t\tconst int base_cur = (i + 1) * np1;\n\t\tconst int base_prev = i * np1;\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tpref[base_cur + (j + 1)] += pref[base_prev + (j + 1)];\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using blocking to improve cache reuse\n\tconst int B = 256; // block size, tuned for typical cache sizes\n\tlong long mxSum = -9223372036854775807LL - 1; // LLONG_MIN\n\n\tfor (int ii = 0; ii < n - s + 1; ii += B) {\n\t\tconst int i_end = std::min(ii + B, n - s + 1);\n\t\tfor (int jj = 0; jj < n - s + 1; jj += B) {\n\t\t\tconst int j_end = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\n\t\t\tfor (int i = ii; i < i_end; ++i) {\n\t\t\t\tconst long long *row_i_s = &pref[(i + s) * np1];\n\t\t\t\tconst long long *row_i   = &pref[i * np1];\n\t\t\t\tfor (int j = jj; j < j_end; ++j) {\n\t\t\t\t\tlong long sum = row_i_s[j + s] - row_i[j + s]\n\t\t\t\t\t               - row_i_s[j] + row_i[j];\n\t\t\t\t\tif (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n\treturn 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using a flat 1D array for matrix storage improves spatial locality during input reading and prefix computation. The two-pass integral image construction (horizontal then vertical) ensures sequential memory access patterns, maximizing cache line utilization. Blocking the submatrix sum search loop further enhances temporal reuse of prefix sums by processing small tiles of top-left corners together.",
  "notes": "The previous flattening attempt failed due to indexing errors; this implementation carefully uses 0-based indices with a (n+1)x(n+1) prefix array and long long for intermediate sums. Block size chosen as 256 for cache efficiency on typical systems.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Flatten matrix from vector-of-vectors to contiguous 1D array",
    "Replace sliding window with integral image (summed-area table) for O(1) submatrix sum queries",
    "Two-pass prefix computation: row-wise cumulative sums then vertical accumulation",
    "Loop blocking on the search loops over top-left corners"
